From 87fe540d7419941fe5d18c38aa429df1ce7fded3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:03:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Power] kodi.log says why Kodi powered off, suspended
 or quit, and who asked

A PC that went down as the TV went off, or that stayed on, could not
be explained from kodi.log: the Standby of CEC, the setting that
decides what it does ("When the TV is switched off") and the power
action itself left no line at the default level, and nothing said
whether a power off came from CEC, a power menu, an add-on, JSON-RPC
or the idle timer.

Each now says itself at INFO:
- CEC: a Standby of the TV, with the setting standby_pc_on_tv_standby,
  its value and what it makes Kodi do, in every case (Ignore too); a
  Standby left alone because Kodi put the TV in standby itself less
  than 20 s before, or because another device sent it.
- The builtins Powerdown(), Shutdown(), Suspend(), Hibernate(),
  Reboot(), RestartApp(), Quit() and RebootToWindows(): the power
  menus of the skins, keys, add-ons and ExecuteBuiltin.
- JSON-RPC System.Shutdown, Suspend, Hibernate and Reboot, and
  Application.Quit.
- The idle timer (it said so at DEBUG only), and what the shutdown
  function is set to.
- The message handler: the action carried out, and a power action of
  CEC that PVR refuses because a recording is running or due.

Nothing changes in what Kodi does. Source check (tools/regress of
LibreELEC, kodi-host fix: power_src_check.py, with seven mutants).
---
